title: October 2024

@suwerenna_merger_decision_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — Ziobro, Jaki, Kaczyński and the organisation's live legal form now emerge from the dynamic result, and every Lewica response retains an outcome-specific political consequence.
title: Suwerenna Polska decides whether to merge with PiS
subtitle: The result follows the organisations' accumulated support and dissent
face-image: img/poland/events/zbigniew-ziobro-2015.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 24
order: 12
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 10 and suwerenna_renamed = 1 and suwerenna_merged = 0 and suwerenna_walkout = 0
on-arrival: {!
const solidarna = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "solidarna";
});
const mergerSupport = Number(Q.suwerenna_merge_support) || 0;
const mergerDissent = Number(Q.suwerenna_merge_dissent) || 0;
Q.suwerenna_individual_joiners = 0;
if (mergerSupport >= 60 && mergerDissent <= 45) {
    Q.suwerenna_merged = 1;
    Q.suwerenna_merger_result = "Full merger into PiS";
    Q.suwerenna_seats = 0;
    if (solidarna) {
        solidarna.active = 0;
        solidarna.kind = "caucus";
        solidarna.allied = 1;
        solidarna.legal_status = "merged current inside PiS";
        solidarna.cohesion = Math.max(58, solidarna.cohesion - 8);
        solidarna.defection_readiness = 0;
    }
    Q.news_headline = "Suwerenna Polska dissolves into PiS after a negotiated vote";
} else if (mergerSupport >= 43 && mergerDissent < 34) {
    Q.suwerenna_merger_result = "Federated United Right agreement";
    Q.suwerenna_seats = 0;
    if (solidarna) {
        solidarna.active = 1;
        solidarna.allied = 1;
        solidarna.legal_status = "federated allied party";
        solidarna.electoral_outside_option = "federated United Right partner";
    }
    Q.news_headline = "Suwerenna Polska keeps its legal identity inside a federation";
} else if (mergerDissent >= 34) {
    Q.suwerenna_merger_result = "Merger refused";
    const independentSeats = Math.min(
        Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.pis_seats) || 0)),
        Math.max(
            0,
            Math.round(Number(solidarna && solidarna.mp_count) || 0)
        )
    );
    Q.suwerenna_seats = independentSeats;
    Q.pis_seats = Math.max(
        0,
        Math.round(Number(Q.pis_seats) || 0) - independentSeats
    );
    Q.suwerenna_seat_ledger_corrected = 1;
    if (
        Q.government_party == "pis" && Q.government_has_confidence &&
        !Q.caretaker_government
    ) {
        Q.government_support_seats = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 0) - independentSeats
        );
        Q.coalition_seats = Math.max(
            0,
            (Number(Q.coalition_seats) || 0) - independentSeats
        );
    }
    if (solidarna) {
        solidarna.active = 1;
        solidarna.allied = 0;
        solidarna.legal_status = "independent party after refused merger";
        solidarna.mp_count = independentSeats;
        solidarna.sejm_mps = independentSeats;
        solidarna.defection_readiness = Math.max(
            65,
            Number(solidarna.defection_readiness) || 0
        );
        solidarna.exclusive_seats = independentSeats;
    }
    Q.news_headline = "Suwerenna Polska refuses the final merger terms";
} else {
    Q.suwerenna_individual_joiners = 4;
    Q.suwerenna_merger_result = "Individual accessions; party survives";
    Q.suwerenna_seats = 0;
    if (solidarna) {
        solidarna.active = 1;
        solidarna.allied = 1;
        solidarna.mp_count = Math.max(0, solidarna.mp_count - 4);
        solidarna.sejm_mps = Math.max(0, solidarna.sejm_mps - 4);
        solidarna.legal_status = "surviving party after individual accessions";
    }
    Q.news_headline = "Four Suwerenna politicians join PiS while the party survives";
}
!}

= October 2024 — [+ suwerenna_merger_result +]

Zbigniew Ziobro's party has taken its own decision after Patryk Jaki negotiated
with Jarosław Kaczyński. **[+ news_headline +].**

[? if suwerenna_merger_result = "Full merger into PiS": The separate treasury,
branches and leadership disappear into PiS; Jaki and the former Justice
Ministry network survive as an organised current under Kaczyński.?][? if
suwerenna_merger_result = "Federated United Right agreement": Suwerenna Polska
keeps its legal identity, officers and bargaining table while promising one
electoral camp with PiS.?][? if suwerenna_merger_result = "Merger refused":
The party keeps its own MPs and organisation outside PiS. Kaczyński has failed
to turn the old coalition into a single opposition machine.?][? if
suwerenna_merger_result = "Individual accessions; party survives": Four
politicians cross to PiS, but Jaki retains a smaller party and the right now has
to explain both loyalty and desertion.?]

Lewica did not choose this organisational result. We choose whether to open a
narrow parliamentary channel, demand one record of accountability, or invite
individual staff and councillors to leave the justice-war inheritance behind.

- @suwerenna_result_nonaggression
- @suwerenna_result_attack
- @suwerenna_result_recruit

@suwerenna_result_nonaggression
title: Offer a vote-by-vote non-aggression channel
subtitle: Test social and institutional votes without endorsing the right's settlement; our own factions will suspect a favour before they see a result.
on-arrival: pis_relation += 2; government_favors += 1; party_unity -= 1; news_headline = "Lewica offers a narrow parliamentary channel after the right's organisational vote"

Our whips offer to discuss named bills rather than a general pact. [? if
suwerenna_merger_result = "Full merger into PiS": The approach goes to one PiS
leadership which now owns Jaki's votes and record together.?][? if
suwerenna_merger_result != "Full merger into PiS": PiS and the surviving
Suwerenna organisation must each decide whether the channel applies to them.?]

The first favour is political access, not a passed law. Party members who spent
years opposing Ziobro see accommodation; potential partners see a Left able to
distinguish a vote from absolution.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the narrow channel on the events desk

@suwerenna_result_attack
title: Attack the settlement as continuity without accountability
subtitle: Join every successor form to Ziobro's justice record; close easier channels to politicians who hoped the new label would clear it.
on-arrival: pis_relation -= 4; progressive_credibility += 3; media_capacity += 1; news_headline = "Lewica makes accountability the argument after the right's settlement"

We publish the prosecutors, disciplinary cases and public offices connecting
Ziobro's old ministry to the organisation which has emerged. A merger cannot
make the record internal, and a federation or refusal cannot make it somebody
else's.

Progressive members recover a clear adversary. Right-wing politicians who
might have sought distance are told that only cooperation with investigations,
not a new party card, can create it.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the accountability record on the events desk

@suwerenna_result_recruit
title: Invite individual social-policy staff and local councillors to talks
subtitle: Recruitment targets named people and local records, not a collective conversion or ownership of Suwerenna Polska.
on-arrival: local_network += 2; labor_credibility += 2; suwerenna_merge_dissent += 3; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "Lewica recruits individuals without claiming ownership of Suwerenna Polska"

Local councillors and policy staff receive invitations based on housing,
benefits and municipal votes rather than loyalty to Jaki or Kaczyński. Nobody
is promised that crossing the room erases a judicial record.

A few conversations strengthen our local network and increase suspicion inside
the surviving hard-right current. We recruit people who can defend a social
record and decline to announce that an entire organisation has moved Left.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the individual talks on the events desk

@migration_pivot_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — the live Prime Minister's turn is situated in the campaign's border record, the government's and opposition's powers diverge, and every response leaves a visible political wound.
title: [+ prime_minister +] proposes suspending territorial asylum access
subtitle: The prime minister asks the democratic camp to cross a line it once condemned
face-image: img/poland/events/donald-tusk-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 27
order: 10
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 10 and government_party = "ko" and caretaker_government = 0 and pm_political_family = "ko"
on-arrival: democratic_rightward_pressure += 5; refugee_empathy -= 3; ko_poll_momentum -= 0.35; left_poll_momentum -= 0.1 if left_in_government = 1; psl_poll_momentum -= 0.1 if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1; p2050_poll_momentum -= 0.1 if ministry_p2050_in_cabinet = 1; public_mood_pending_border_security_support += 10; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += -10; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_salience += 14; news_headline = "The prime minister's migration turn forces the Left to choose its coalition limit"

= October 2024 — A government line the Left did not write

Prime Minister **[+ prime_minister +]** of **[+ pm_party_name +]**, heading the
KO-led coalition, proposes a
temporary suspension of the right to lodge asylum claims at parts of the
Belarusian frontier. Border officers ask for a rule they can enforce. Asylum
lawyers warn that a government cannot make an individual right disappear by
calling the pressure at the border exceptional.

The proposal arrives after the state adopted **[+ border_doctrine +]** at the
frontier and Lewica argued for **[+ refugee_settlement +]** in receiving
communities. **Anna Maria Żukowska**, chair of Lewica's parliamentary club,
must now decide whether those words describe a limit or merely an aspiration.
[? if left_in_government = 1: Our ministers can put their offices behind an
ultimatum, dissent inside the cabinet, or accept safeguards which narrow the
suspension without removing it.?]
[? if left_in_government = 0: We hold no cabinet office to resign. Our leverage
is an opposition amendment, a public standard and the votes the prime minister still needs
to defend his turn.?]

- @migration_resign
- @migration_dissent
- @migration_conditions
- @migration_opposition

@migration_resign
title: Threaten resignation unless the suspension is withdrawn
subtitle: Make asylum law a test of whether Lewica can remain in this cabinet.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: asylum_position_2025 = "Withdrawal threat against suspension"; coalition_break_threat = 1; ko_relation -= 12; psl_relation -= 4; p2050_relation += 2; progressive_credibility += 5; government_coalition_dissent += 12; early_election_risk += 8; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += 9; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_salience += 10; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_backlash += 7; news_headline = "The asylum plan becomes a coalition survival question"

Lewica's ministers put resignation letters on the table before the cabinet
meeting. The prime minister can withdraw the suspension, find a majority
without us, or let
the dispute become an early-election question. Rights organisations finally
hear an unambiguous limit; our coalition partners hear a threat to the
government they assembled only a year ago.

- @poland_event_queue: Leave the resignation letters on the events desk

@migration_dissent
title: Vote against it while remaining in government
subtitle: Keep the ministries, but make the cabinet expose its own divided majority.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: asylum_position_2025 = "Coalition dissent against suspension"; border_rights_standard += 5; progressive_credibility += 4; ko_relation -= 6; government_coalition_dissent += 5; razem_cooperation += 3; public_trust -= 2; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += 9; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_backlash += 4; news_headline = "Lewica records a government dissent on asylum"

Our ministers stay, and Lewica's deputies vote no. The parliamentary record
gives lawyers and Razem a line they can cite, but it also leaves the public
with two government positions at once: a suspension announced by the prime
minister and rejected by one of his governing parties. We preserve both our
offices and our objection, at the cost of making each look less decisive.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the recorded dissent on the events desk

@migration_conditions
title: Demand a time limit, judicial review and humanitarian access
subtitle: Narrow the suspension in law while accepting that some suspension will pass.
on-arrival: asylum_position_2025 = "Time limit, review and humanitarian access"; border_rights_standard += 3; constitutional_restraint += 4; ko_relation += 1; psl_relation += 1; progressives_dissent += 2; razem_dissent += 3; public_trust += 1; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += 8; public_mood_pending_border_security_support += 3; news_headline = "Procedural safeguards narrow but do not remove the asylum suspension"

The draft returns with an expiry date, access for humanitarian workers and a
route to judicial review. Border officers receive a bounded emergency power
rather than an open-ended instruction. The prime minister accepts the restraints and calls
the bill responsible; refugee advocates answer that Lewica has helped make a
suspension lawful instead of stopping it.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the amended suspension on the events desk

@migration_opposition
title: Table a rights-and-review amendment from opposition
subtitle: Lewica can amend and scrutinise the bill, not threaten to resign from a cabinet it does not serve.
view-if: left_in_government = 0
on-arrival: asylum_position_2025 = "Opposition amendment for review and humanitarian access"; border_rights_standard += 4; constitutional_restraint += 3; ko_relation -= 2; razem_cooperation += 2; public_trust += 1; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += 10; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_salience += 8; public_mood_pending_border_security_support -= 3; news_headline = "Lewica records an opposition alternative to the asylum suspension"

Żukowska files a competing text: individual assessment remains the rule,
courts retain review and humanitarian organisations regain access. KO must
now reject those protections in public or borrow them from an opposition it
has spent the week blaming for obstruction. We cannot command the cabinet,
but we can make its choice legible.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the opposition amendment on the events desk

@razem_split_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — The split is a conflict among identifiable people over office and delivery, with separate parliamentary and organisational consequences retained after every choice.
title: Razem prepares to leave
subtitle: Five parliamentarians choose cooperation; the party chooses opposition
face-image: img/poland/events/adrian-zandberg-2020.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 27
order: 11
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2024 and month = 10 and razem_split = 0 and razem_breakaway_protected = 0 and government_party != "pis"
on-arrival: news_headline = "Housing, health and coalition responsibility split Razem"

= October 2024 — One party becomes three relationships

<span class="party-razem"><b>Adrian Zandberg</b></span>, Razem's co-founder and leading parliamentary voice, says
that remaining tied to a democratic government without decisive gains in
housing, health or abortion law has become complicity. Senate deputy marshal
**Magdalena Biejat** and Sejm deputies **Daria Gosek-Popiołek**, **Dorota
Olko**, **Joanna Wicha** and **Marta Stożek** answer that permanent opposition
is not a theory of power. They are prepared to leave the party rather than
abandon cooperation.

If no agreement survives tonight, Razem becomes an independent opposition
organisation while the five parliamentarians remain a cooperative current
beside New Left. [? if left_in_government = 1: Our ministers keep their
portfolios, but they lose the claim that the younger left entered government
as one camp.?] [? if left_in_government = 0: We are already outside the
cabinet; the rupture would divide an opposition that has little institutional
leverage to spare.?]

The abortion defeat is now part of that trust test. The party promised **[+
movement_reckoning_result +]**. [? if abortion_cabinet_deadline = 1: Razem can
measure the promised spring vote against cabinet participation; another vague
programme guarantee will not substitute for it.?]

- @razem_historical
- @razem_protocol
- @razem_absorb

@razem_historical
title: Accept the split and negotiate orderly parliamentary separation
subtitle: Let Zandberg take the party into opposition while the cooperative current remains beside New Left.
on-arrival: {!
const razemCurrentSeats = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.round(Number(Q.razem_seats) || 0)
);
const cooperativeSejmSeats = Math.min(4, razemCurrentSeats);
const oppositionSeats = Math.max(
    0,
    razemCurrentSeats - cooperativeSejmSeats
);
const currentRazemStrength = Math.max(0, Number(Q.razem_strength) || 0);
const cooperativeStrength = currentRazemStrength * (
    razemCurrentSeats > 0
        ? cooperativeSejmSeats / razemCurrentSeats
        : 0.4
);
const razemExitStrength = Math.max(
    0,
    currentRazemStrength - cooperativeStrength
);
const currentProgressiveStrength = Math.max(
    0,
    Number(Q.progressives_strength) || 0
);
const combinedProgressiveStrength =
    currentProgressiveStrength + cooperativeStrength;
const cooperativeDissent = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.razem_dissent) || 0) - 8
);
Q.razem_split = 1;
Q.razem_split_outcome = "historical";
Q.razem_cooperation_protocol = 0;
Q.razem_breakaway_protected = 0;
Q.razem_in_left_club = 0;
Q.razem_opposition_circle = 1;
Q.razem_active = 0;
Q.razem_in_left = 0;
Q.razem_party_formed = 1;
Q.razem_party_relation = 42;
Q.razem_exit_strength = razemExitStrength;
Q.razem_strength = 0;
Q.razem_dissent = 0;
Q.razem_escalation_stage = 7;
Q.razem_circle_formed = 1;
Q.razem_mp_departed = oppositionSeats;
Q.razem_mp_retained = cooperativeSejmSeats;
Q.progressives_strength = combinedProgressiveStrength;
Q.progressives_dissent = combinedProgressiveStrength > 0
    ? (
        currentProgressiveStrength *
            Math.max(0, Number(Q.progressives_dissent) || 0) +
        cooperativeStrength * cooperativeDissent
    ) / combinedProgressiveStrength
    : 0;
Q.progressives_name = "Wspólne Jutro";
Q.progressives_leader = "Magdalena Biejat";
Q.progressives_broker = "Biejat and the cooperative former Razem MPs";
Q.progressives_active = 1;
Q.progressives_in_left = 1;
Q.wspolne_jutro_formed = 1;
Q.wspolne_jutro_outcome =
    "Biejat-led cooperative current inside the Left";
Q.razem_leader = "Adrian Zandberg";
Q.razem_co_leader = "Vacant";
Q.razem_leadership_result =
    "Zandberg chairs independent Razem after Biejat's departure";
Q.biejat_party = "Wspólne Jutro";
Q.gosek_popiolek_party = "Wspólne Jutro";
Q.olko_party = "Wspólne Jutro";
Q.wicha_party = "Wspólne Jutro";
Q.stozek_party = "Wspólne Jutro";
Q.razem_biejat_relation = 42;
Q.party_unity -= 8;
Q.razem_cooperation = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.razem_cooperation) || 0) - 10
);
Q.barons_dissent += 2;
Q.spring_dissent -= 1;
Q.labor_dissent -= 2;
Q.pps_dissent += 2;
Q.left_seats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_seats) - oppositionSeats);
Q.razem_party_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.razem_party_seats) || 0) + oppositionSeats;
Q.left_cooperative_independent_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_cooperative_independent_seats) || 0) +
    cooperativeSejmSeats;
Q.left_progressives_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_progressives_seats) || 0) +
    cooperativeSejmSeats;
Q.left_new_generation_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_labor_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_progressives_seats) || 0);
Q.razem_seats = 0;
Q.zandberg_advisor = 0;
Q.zawisza_advisor = 0;
Q.matysiak_advisor = 0;
Q.seat_subvention_seats = Q.left_seats;
Q.news_headline = Q.left_in_government
    ? "Razem leaves the club while its cooperative minority remains with the governing left"
    : "Razem separates from Lewica while its cooperative minority remains in the common opposition club";
!}

The meeting ends with two sets of keys and two political addresses. Zandberg
takes Razem's organisation, its dissident current and its claim to an
uncompromised opposition. Biejat and the four Sejm deputies keep working with
New Left, but no longer speak for Razem.

Zandberg, **Marcelina Zawisza** and <span class="party-razem"><b>Paulina Matysiak</b></span> leave our internal
councils with the party. [? if left_in_government = 1: The cabinet survives;
its left flank is smaller and now has an organised critic outside it.?]
[? if left_in_government = 0: The parliamentary opposition survives, but the
same voters are now courted by rival organisations with rival accounts of why
Lewica failed to deliver.?]

The SLD barons value the four retained Sejm votes; Wiosna veterans recognise a
bridge rather than a new rival party. Lewica Pracy MPs and union organisers
welcome Biejat's housing-and-care voice, the progressive current gives
**Wspólne Jutro** its name and leadership, and PPS warns that cooperation
without an autonomous party can still become dependence.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the separation agreement on the events desk

@razem_protocol
title: Offer funded milestones and a binding outside-support protocol
subtitle: Spend 2 resources on deadlines Razem can enforce without surrendering its autonomy.
choose-if: resources >= 2 and razem_cooperation >= 48 and party_unity >= 42
unavailable-subtitle: Too little trust remains for another paper settlement.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 2;
Q.razem_split = 0;
Q.razem_split_outcome = "protocol";
Q.razem_cooperation_protocol = 1;
Q.razem_breakaway_protected = 1;
Q.razem_active = 1;
Q.razem_in_left = 1;
Q.razem_in_left_club = 1;
Q.razem_party_formed = 0;
Q.razem_opposition_circle = 0;
Q.razem_dissent = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.razem_dissent) || 0) - 12);
Q.razem_cooperation = Math.min(
    100,
    (Number(Q.razem_cooperation) || 0) + 8
);
Q.razem_biejat_relation = Math.min(
    100,
    (Number(Q.razem_biejat_relation) || 52) + 12
);
Q.razem_leader = "Adrian Zandberg";
Q.razem_co_leader = "Magdalena Biejat";
Q.razem_leadership_result =
    "Zandberg and Biejat co-chair Razem under a binding cooperation protocol";
Q.biejat_party = "Razem";
Q.gosek_popiolek_party = "Razem";
Q.olko_party = "Razem";
Q.wicha_party = "Razem";
Q.stozek_party = "Razem";
Q.wspolne_jutro_formed = 0;
Q.wspolne_jutro_outcome = "Rupture prevented by the binding Razem protocol";
Q.budget_promises += 3;
Q.ko_relation -= 4;
Q.psl_relation -= 3;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 4;
Q.party_unity += 4;
Q.barons_dissent += 4;
Q.spring_dissent -= 1;
Q.labor_dissent -= 2;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 2;
Q.pps_dissent -= 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "A binding support protocol prevents the Left's expected rupture";
!}

The signatures sit beneath funded housing and health milestones, an abortion
vote date and a clause allowing Razem to oppose the government outside that
programme. Zandberg postpones the departure because the paper now contains
dates and money, not another appeal to unity. KO and PSL see a second coalition
agreement written for a party which still reserves the right to vote against
them.

The SLD barons resent the enforceable veto, while Wiosna veterans accept the
price of unity. Labour and the progressives claim the funded milestones and
rights deadline; PPS treats the appeal clause as a useful guarantee that a
smaller socialist partner can remain itself.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the signed support protocol on the events desk

@razem_absorb
title: Bring the cooperative five into New Left and isolate Zandberg
subtitle: Gain parliamentarians and media discipline by turning an argument over strategy into a fight over capture.
